  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8d1e7c28-9f24-4ac6-8d43-3ab1d2a80d01",
    "name": "Discord DMs — CPR Lab 3 (Gateway + Redis + Discovery)",
    "description": "CPR-integrated version combining the supplied Discord DMs Lab 3 Discovery tests with Gateway auth/negotiation and real player/session setup.\n\nIn CPR: base_url=http://localhost:8090 (API Gateway), discord_proxy_url=http://localhost:8086 (Traefik). Discord DMs itself is not bound directly to host port 3000. Discovery checks require discovery_url=http://localhost:18000 to be safely forwarded from the Docker network (not published by default).\n\nOrder: Run 0 Setup; 1 Gateway WebSocket Negotiation; 4 Socket.IO Preparation; then use two Postman Socket.IO requests with the socketio_url and emit join_channel/send_message as described by the Lab 3 cross-replica folder. REST Channels/Messages and Service Discovery tests can be run independently where their variables exist.\n\nThe JSON Postman Collection v2.1 export contains HTTP requests and manual instructions; it does NOT contain native Postman Socket.IO request tabs. Redis connection logs alone do not establish successful cross-replica event delivery.\n\nThe legacy 'Provision Session Channels' request is preserved but must not be considered a validated current integration without checking the Session workflow.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
