      "description": "Manual cross-replica Socket.IO test (HTTP collection export cannot store Socket.IO request tabs):\n1. Run Setup, Gateway WebSocket Negotiation, and Socket.IO Preparation.\n2. Run `curl -i http://localhost:8086/health` without cookies until you see two instance IDs. Save each response's `Set-Cookie: discord_route=...` value.\n3. Create two Socket.IO requests in Postman to {{socketio_url}} (not HTTP requests). In their handshake headers use different `Cookie: discord_route=<cookie>` values, targeting different replicas.\n4. Connect both. Moderator emits `join_channel` with {\"channel_id\":\"{{socket_channel_id}}\",\"player_id\":\"{{player_id}}\"}.\n5. Junior emits `join_channel` with {\"channel_id\":\"{{socket_channel_id}}\",\"player_id\":\"{{junior_player_id}}\"}.\n6. On Junior, listen to the server event `message`. On Moderator, emit `send_message` with {\"channel_id\":\"{{socket_channel_id}}\",\"sender_id\":\"{{player_id}}\",\"content\":\"Lab 3 cross-replica test\"}.\n7. Verify the junior receives the message while connected to the other replica. This is the real Redis cross-instance test.\n8. Redis adapter startup logs or successful HTTP requests alone do not prove event delivery.",
